ndon't think git-annex contains infinite retry loops, but if sqlite fails\nwith ErrorBusy, it will indeed retry as long as that error persists.\n\nThat said, it has 7 of the 8 downloads apparently started to the point\nof opening destination files, and I don't see how the export db could\nblock a download from running/failing once it's reached that point. All\nexport db querying happens before it's opened the destination file. So\nit seems something else has made those download threads get stuck.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1568033761,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyOTQ2MDE2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3613#issuecomment-529460163"},"message":"\u003e Is the remote it would be getting files from an export remote? And what type of remote is it?\n\nyes, should be exported to S3 (public).  Original dataset is here: https://github.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds002000","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1568128199,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyOTk4MjEyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3613#issuecomment-529982121"},"message":"Could you tar up the deleted files, so I can examine their contents?\n\ntar hcvf deleted-files.tar /proc/3671312/fd\n\n(h to follow the links, should get the content)\n\nAfter that I think all that's left to try is destructive changes.\nIf you strace the process to a log, and start killing its child git\nprocesses one by one, any change in behavior might provide a hint about\nwhat it's stuck on, in case it involves communication with them.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1568128575,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyOTk4NTAyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3613#issuecomment-529985023"},"message":"ok - tarball is at /tmp/deleted-files.tar on smaug and now you can play \"being Yarik\" game -- your authorized ssh keys are allowed to login as me so you could do as much evil to that process as you see helpful.  Just please let me know when you are done ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1568139747,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMDA2MDY2Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3613#issuecomment-530060662"},"message":"The export database is consistent and sqlite has flushed the write-ahead\nlog into it already. I don't think sqlite is involved.\n\nOne interesting thing is fd 2 which was being redirected to a file that\ngot deleted, and ends like this:\n\ndownload failed: Forbidden\ndownload failed: Forbidden\ndownload failed: \u003cstdout\u003e: hPutBuf: resource vanished (Broken pipe)\n\nThe write to stdout seemed to fail at the same time it was outputting\nthe last \"download failed\" to stderr, leading to intermingled output.\nStrange that it's not finished outputting the http error message. The\ncode flushes it:\n\n                        hPutStrLn stderr $ \"download failed: \" ++ msg\n                        hFlush stderr\n\nPerhaps it somehow hung while extracting the http error message.\n\nAlso noticed that the process has ballooned to 2.8 gb of memory. That is\nnot normal for a git-annex get. It does not seem to be growing any\nfurther when I let the process run. Took a memory dump.\n\nKilling the git cat-files did not change the behavior, so it was not\ntrying to communicate with those. I've killed the process entirely now.\nIt never output anything more to stderr.\n\nDon't know what to make of this.. Archived everything in\nlib/big/git-annex-data-from-users/yoh-left-behind/\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1568140452,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMDA2N